{"event": "artifact", "agent": "documentation", "file": "README.md", "content": "# Todo List\n\nA simple in-memory todo service implemented in Python.\n\n## Purpose\n\nThis project provides a basic implementation of a todo list using Python. It includes functions to create, retrieve, list, mark as complete, and delete todos without using a database.\n\n## API\n\n### Required Module-Level Functions\n\n#### `create_todo(title)`\n- **Parameters**: \n  - `title` (str): The title of the todo.\n- **Returns**: None\n- **Raises**:\n  - `ValueError`: If the title is empty or whitespace.\n\n#### `get_todo(todo_id)`\n- **Parameters**: \n  - `todo_id` (int): The ID of the todo to retrieve.\n- **Returns**: A dictionary representing the todo.\n- **Raises**:\n  - `KeyError`: If the todo with the given ID does not exist.\n\n#### `list_todos()`\n- **Parameters**: None\n- **Returns**: A list of dictionaries representing all todos.\n\n#### `complete_todo(todo_id)`\n- **Parameters**: \n  - `todo_id` (int): The ID of the todo to mark as complete.\n- **Returns**: None\n- **Raises**:\n  - `KeyError`: If the todo with the given ID does not exist.\n\n#### `delete_todo(todo_id)`\n- **Parameters**: \n  - `todo_id` (int): The ID of the todo to delete.\n- **Returns**: A dictionary representing the deleted todo.\n- **Raises**:\n  - `KeyError`: If the todo with the given ID does not exist.\n\n## Simple Usage Example\n\n```python\nfrom app import create_todo, get_todo, list_todos, complete_todo, delete_todo\n\n# Create a new todo\ncreate_todo(\"Buy groceries\")\n\n# List all todos\nprint(list_todos())\n\n# Complete a todo\ncomplete_todo(1)\n\n# Get a specific todo\nprint(get_todo(1))\n\n# Delete a todo\ndeleted_todo = delete_todo(1)\nprint(deleted_todo)\n```\n\n## How to Run Pytest\n\nTo run the tests, ensure you have `pytest` installed. You can install it using pip if you haven't already:\n\n```sh\npip install pytest\n```\n\nThen, navigate to the directory containing your test files and run:\n\n```sh\npytest\n```\n\nThis will execute all the tests defined in your test files."}
